Next, create a new file named `.eslintrc.json` in the root of your project and add the following configuration:
```json
{
  "env": {
    "browser": true,
    "es6": true
  },
  "extends": "react-native",
  "rules": {
    "quotes": ["error", "single"],
    "semi": ["error", "always"]
  },
  "globals": {
    "Atomics": "readonly",
    "SharedArrayBuffer": "readonly"
  }
}
```
This configuration tells ESLint to use the React Native preset, enable browser globals (e.g. `window`), and enforce single quotes and semi-colons.

